---
description: Call git by absolute OS path so commits are not rewritten with disallowed trailers
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git binary

Do not run the bare `git` command. The agent shell intercepts `git` and appends trailers such as `Co-authored-by: Cursor`. This repository rejects those trailers.

Call git by an absolute path to the OS install. Resolve the path once per session. Reuse that path for every git invocation.

Do not use a binary whose path contains `Cursor`, `cursor-agent`, or another editor wrapper.

## Resolve the binary

macOS and Linux (bash/zsh):

```sh
if [ -x /usr/bin/git ]; then GIT=/usr/bin/git
elif [ -x /usr/local/bin/git ]; then GIT=/usr/local/bin/git
elif [ -x /opt/homebrew/bin/git ]; then GIT=/opt/homebrew/bin/git
else echo 'No system git found' >&2; exit 1
fi
"$GIT" status
```

Windows PowerShell:

```powershell
$git = @(
  "$env:ProgramFiles\Git\cmd\git.exe",
  "${env:ProgramFiles(x86)}\Git\cmd\git.exe",
  "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Programs\Git\cmd\git.exe"
) | Where-Object { Test-Path $_ } | Select-Object -First 1
if (-not $git) { throw 'No system git found' }
& $git status
```

Windows cmd:

```bat
if exist "%ProgramFiles%\Git\cmd\git.exe" ("%ProgramFiles%\Git\cmd\git.exe" status) else if exist "%ProgramFiles(x86)%\Git\cmd\git.exe" ("%ProgramFiles(x86)%\Git\cmd\git.exe" status) else (echo No system git found & exit /b 1)
```

## Commits

Keep hooks enabled. Do not pass `--no-verify`, `--no-gpg-sign`, or equivalent.

Commit messages must match commitlint:

- Conventional type and subject only (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `test:`, `docs:`).
- No body. `body-max-length` is 0.
- No `Co-authored-by`, `Generated with`, or `Made-with` trailers.

```sh
# BAD — intercepted; trailer is added
git commit -m "feat: native discovery"

# GOOD — absolute path; message stays intact
"$GIT" commit -m "feat: native discovery"
```
